ba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/eha-kick-off-grant\", \"text\": \"EHA Kick-off Grant\", \"source_region\": \"main\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 4573, \"end\": 4753, \"text\": \"ants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nIn this section, you can also learn about EHA Travel Grants, funding from\"}}], \"supported_parent_doc_ids\": [], \"source_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-cbefd1c2c3a09225cc1843c0\", \"title\": \"Specialized Working Groups - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Specialized Working Groups - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4054, \"end\": 4080, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 26}, {\"start\": 4135, \"end\": 5709, \"excerpt_start\": 27, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Specialized Working Groups\\nEHA’s Specialized Working Groups (SWGs) foster science and spread knowledge in basic, translational, and clinical research in hematology.\\nTo ensure we cover the full field of hematology and provide a research platform for all groups and researchers, we’ve established two types of SWG:\\nDisease-oriented SWGs—which cover specific topics such as leukemias and lymphomas\\nOverarching SWGs—which cover broad themes such as aging and precision medicine\\nThis model is based on the nine sections of the EHA Roadmap for European Hematology Research.\\nThere are currently 25 SWGs. You can use the filter below to view them by type.\\nHow to join an SWG\\nIf you’re interested in making new connections or sharing your expertise, you can apply to join an SWG. To do this, just follow the instructions on the main page of the relevant SWG.\\nSWG Grants\\nEHA provides financial support to small research projects initiated by our SWGs. You can find out more about his support, and discover some of the projects we’ve already supported, in the SWG Grants section.\\nEHA Lymphoma Group\\nEuropean Research Initiative on CLL (ERIC)\\nEuropean Scientific foundation for Laboratory Hemato Oncology (ESLHO)\\nOverarching Specialized Working Group on Diagnostics in Hematology\\nSpecialized Working Group on Acute Myeloid Leukemia\\nSpecialized Working Group on Adolescents and Young Adults with Hematologic Diseases (AYA)\\nSpecialized Working Group on Adult Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia\\nSpecialized Working Group on Aging and Hematology\\nSpecialized Working Group on Bleeding and Thrombosis\\nSpecialized Working Grou\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-88851fc8d85e155717517ebd\", \"title\": \"HemaSphere - The European Hematology Association (EHA)HemaSphere - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3990, \"end\": 4000, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 10}, {\"start\": 4039, \"end\": 4100, \"excerpt_start\": 11, \"excerpt_end\": 72}, {\"start\": 4192, \"end\": 5721, \"excerpt_start\": 73, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"HemaSphere\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · April 30, 2025\\nApril 30, 2025\\nShare\\nStay at the forefront of cutting-edge research with EHA’s open access, peer-reviewed journal.\\nWith a preliminary 2025 Impact Factor of 11.3, placing it #8 in indexed hematology journals worldwide, HemaSphere is an invaluable resource for hematologists at every career stage.\\nOur continuous online publications support the global hematology community by sharing:\\nResults of high-impact basic, translational, and clinical hematology research\\nInsightful review articles\\nClinical practice guidelines\\nReports of new therapies\\nRecommendations for future research and clinical applications\\nDiscussions on European policy\\nAnd more\\nWe also provide the hematology community with a friction-free route to publishing and publication access through our:\\nFast and constructive review process\\n100% open access content\\nLow publication fees\\nLatest issue\\nExplore this month’s HemaSphere issue, featuring a broad range of hematology papers and insightful discussions on trending topics.\\nHemaSphere podcast\\nListen to the latest HemaSphere podcast and enjoy lighthearted conversations about the research stories behind the publications.\\nThis audio companion to our official journal is available on a range of podcast platforms, and we launch new episodes regularly.\\nCall for novel findings\\nHemaSphere is interested in high-impact studies that share novel findings.\\nIf your study fits this description, please feel free to submit it online for our consideration. HemaSphere does not charge any submission fees.\\nDiscounted publishing fees for EHA membe\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-9e620f66ae71fe39b118f492\", \"title\": \"About EHA - The European Hematology Association (EHA)About EHA - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3986, \"end\": 4480, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 494}, {\"start\": 4721, \"end\": 4741, \"excerpt_start\": 495, \"excerpt_end\": 515}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"About EHA\\nMission and vision\\nBoard and committees\\nExecutive Office\\nEuropean affairs\\nCompliance, plans, and reports\\nPartnerships\\nWork at EHA\\nEHA Awards\\nGet involved\\nNews & updates\\n“Borderless Hematology is about giving the best quality of care to all hematology patients.”\\nProf Antonio Almeida, Past EHA President\\nHospital da Luz, Lisbon\\n“Borderless Hematology is about giving the best quality of care to all hematology patients.”\\nProf Antonio Almeida, Past EHA President\\nHospital da Luz, Lisbon\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-b6c9d3593c6121cf0281911b\", \"title\": \"2026 winners - The European Hematology Association (EHA)2026 winners - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4069, \"end\": 4126, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 57}, {\"start\": 4231, \"end\": 5774, \"excerpt_start\": 58, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n8 min read · June 2, 2026\\nJune 2, 2026\\nShare\\n2026 winners\\nJunior Research Grant\\nMartina Sarchi, University of Pavia, Italy\\nTopic: ExIT-SF3B1: cell Extrinsic and Intrinsic mis-splicing-induced mechanisms and Therapeutic targets in SF3B1-mutant myelodysplastic neoplasms\\nPetr Danek, Institute of Organic Chemistry and Biochemistry of the CAS, Czechia\\nTopic: Chemically altered undigestible DNA: the driver of adverse effects associated with Busulfan/Cyclophosphamide treatment\\nNoémie Jollive, EFS INSERM U1255, France\\nTopic: Mechanobiology of the Blood-Bone Marrow Barrier after Pre-Transplant Conditioning and Its Role in HSPC Homing\\nPaula Rodriguez Marques, Amsterdam University Medical Center, The Netherlands\\nTopic: CAR-T Associated hematotoxicity: Resolving Mechanisms to reveal therapeutic Approaches\\nAdvanced Research Grant\\nAlyssa Cull, University of York, United Kingdom\\nTopic: Fanning the Flames: Characterising the Role of Macrophages in Blood Cancer Development\\nFranziska Auer, Technical University Munich, University Hospital, Germany\\nTopic: Determinants of Leukemia Predisposition and Therapy Resistance in PAX5-Driven B-ALL\\nMarlies Vanden Bempt, KU Leuven, Belgium\\nTopic: EZH2 mutations in clonal hematopoiesis and ETP-like ALL: a common mechanism?\\nPhysician Scientist Research Grant\\nNikolett Wohner, Semmelweis University, Hungary\\nTopic: Neutrophil Extracellular Traps: Basic Mechanisms and Clinical Implications\\nEtienne Crickx, Henri Mondor Hospital, France\\nTopic: Exploring humoral responses in delayed hemolytic transfusion reactions\\nFederica Barzaghi, IRCCS Ospedale San \"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"title\": \"EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4026, \"end\": 4045, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 19}, {\"start\": 4100, \"end\": 4159, \"excerpt_start\": 20, \"excerpt_end\": 79}, {\"start\": 4536, \"end\": 6058, \"excerpt_start\": 80, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Research Grants\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · June 16, 2026\\nJune 16, 2026\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Research Grants are designed to support the future of hematology by helping talented junior researchers to:\\nConduct basic or translational lab-based research\\nGain valuable research and leadership experience\\nMove towards becoming group leaders\\nAdvance their careers\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nYou’re an EHA member\\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\\nYou have the support of an academic department and institute\\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\\nTypes of EHA Research Grants\\nThe three types of EHA Research Grant are the:\\nEHA Junior Research Grant, which can provide up to €150,000 for three years\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEach one of the three types of EHA Research Grant also has its own specific eligibility criteria. Please make sure you read the eligibility criteria for your grant type before you apply.\\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the sele\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4142, \"end\": 5742, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership.\\nWelcome to Borderless Hematology.\\nEHA is the leading force in hematology, bringing the community together to share knowledge, collaborate, connect, and grow.\\nTogether we accelerate progress through education, science, and innovation. Together we improve patient outcomes and progress towards cures—across Europe and beyond.\\nTogether, the future of hematology is within our reach.\\nJoin us with membership that works for you or learn more about our story.\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEuropean affairs\\nEHA Campus\\nGrants\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nWhat’s new?\\nGo to overview\\nTuesday, September 29, 2026\\nEHA's Long-Term Advocacy for Hematology Achieves a Major Milestone\\nTuesday, September 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Ariane Weinman\\nThursday, July 23, 2026\\nASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase\\nWednesday, July 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Kate Morgan\\nMonday, July 6, 2026\\nPublication of EHA Annual General Meeting 2026 minutes\\nReady to join our community?\\nOur network is not just a professional association; it’s a community that nurtures growth, membership, and innovation in a manner that transcends geographical and intellectual borders. To us, this is Borderless Hematology.\\nJoin EHA today\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nBecome a mentor today\\nMentoring is about more than sharing knowledge. It’s about building connections, gaining fresh perspectives, and helping shape the future of hematology.\\nIf you believe in the power of community and want to suppo\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"title\": \"Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3974, \"end\": 5007, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1033}, {\"start\": 5248, \"end\": 5268, \"excerpt_start\": 1034, \"excerpt_end\": 1054}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Grants\\nEHA’s foundations are built upon our belief that it’s the collective endeavors of our community—in research and clinical practice—that lead to exponential advancements.\\nWe’re committed to accelerating progress in hematology by promoting collaboration, education, and research across all levels.\\nAn important way of achieving this is through the careful and selective allocation of grants and funding to aspiring scientists and researchers.\\nTo check which of our grants you can apply for, use the filters below. Alternatively, you can read about our different grant categories:\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nIn this section, you can also learn about EHA Travel Grants, funding from non-EHA sources and browse our grant-winners hall of fame.\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Junior Research Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}], \"local_exploration\": {\"visited_doc_ids\": [\"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"web-740265f7f67c3ce2a194ca41\", \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"web-b6c9d3593c6121cf0281911b\", \"web-fa499d75bb6176a42b1557b3\", \"web-9e620f66ae71fe39b118f492\", \"web-9bdd70664e43e95f6f2247c0\", \"web-88851fc8d85e155717517ebd\", \"web-cbefd1c2c3a09225cc1843c0\"], \"visited_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and par